\begin_layout Subsection*
Part C
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Question:
\series default
 Are the results in (b) consistent with the fact that the treatment was
 randomly assigned conditional on school of attendance? Explain.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

If treatment was randomly assigned conditional on school of attendance,
 then we should see no signifianct differences amongst the relevant control
 variables across treatment status.
 Now, conditional on school of attendance, we fail to reject the null hypothesis
 at the 5% level for the three major control variables of students (free
 lunch, white/asian, age in 1985).
 Thus, when restricting our attention to new STAR participants only in each
 of kindergarten, 1st grade, 2nd grade, and 3rd grade, treatment was randomly
 assigned contional on school of attendance.
\end_layout

