\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Question: 
\series default
Interpret the coefficients on the small class and regular/aide class indicators
 in the first specification.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Kindergarten
\series default
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

The small and regular/aide class indicators have coefficients of 4.768 and
 -0.195, respectively.
 The coefficient on the small class is significant at the 0.1% level, while
 the coefficient on the regular/aide class is not significant at the standard
 5% level.
 The constant term is 49.15, and it is significant at the 0.1% level.
 Thus, on average, the kindergarten students in the small class had an average
 percentile score of 53.918, students in the regular class had an average
 percentile score of 49.15, and those in the regular class with an aide has
 an average percentile score of 48.955.
\end_layout

