\begin_layout Subsection*
Part C
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Question: 
\series default
How do the coefficients on the small class and regular/aide class indicators
 change as more covariates are added to the model?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Kindergarten
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

The coefficient on the small class indicator increases when I control for
 school fixed effects, and they relatively remain the same when I add the
 control variables associated with student characteristics.
 Yet, the coefficient slightly decreases when I add the control variables
 associated with teacher characteristics.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

The coefficient on the regular/aide class indicator increases when I control
 for school fixed effects.
 In fact, the coefficient even becomes positive.
 When I add the control variables associated with student characteristics,
 the coefficient increases once again, yet it decreases drastically when
 I add the control variables associated with teacher characteristics.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
First grade
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

The coefficients on both the small class and regular/aide class indicators
 decrease consistently when I control for school fixed effects and add the
 control variables associated with student and teacher characteristics.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Second grade
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

The coefficients on the small class indicator increases when I control for
 school fixed effects.
 Yet, the coefficient decreases when I add the control variables associated
 with student and teacher characteristics.
 The coefficient on the regular/aide class follows the same pattern in the
 first two specifications.
 When I add the control variables associated with student characteristics,
 the coefficient increases once again.
 However, the coefficient decreases below the magnitude of the second specificat
ion when I add the control variables associated with teacher characteristics.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Third grade
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
